  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "I know that earmuff mode is a thing, but it is not able to adjust the voice volume of a user when they are up close. This can be frustrating when someone suddenly starts blasting audio at max volume even though you set up earmuff mode. A possible solution is to introduce a local volume limiter toggle, so that if a nearby user is shouting or playing loud audio, it will automatically lower their volume to more comfortable levels then return the volume back to normal once the audio levels go below a specific threshold after a short delay.",
